.TH FILE-ENUMERATOR 1 "July 2026" "file-enumerator 1.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
file-enumerator \- recursively inventory files and supported archive members
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B file-enumerator
.RI [ options ]
.I ROOT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B file-enumerator
walks
.I ROOT
and its subdirectories, applies optional file-extension, filename, and folder
filters, and writes the matching inventory as text, CSV, or both.
.PP
Supported ZIP and TAR-family archives are inspected by default without
extracting their contents. Archive members are evaluated by the same filters as
filesystem files and are clearly marked in generated reports.
.PP
Exclusions always win. Multiple values within one filter category are treated
as OR conditions. Different include categories are combined as AND conditions.
For example, when both an included extension and an included folder are given,
a file must satisfy both filters.
.PP
Matching is case-insensitive by default. Filename and folder filters use
shell-style glob patterns including
.BR * ,
.BR ? ,
and character ranges such as
.BR [0-9] .
Folder patterns match either an individual folder component or the relative
folder path beneath
.IR ROOT .
Archives act as virtual folders for folder-filter matching.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I ROOT
Root directory to enumerate.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --include-filetype " TYPE"
.TQ
.BR --include-ext " TYPE"
Include files with the specified extension. Accepts forms such as
.BR pdf ,
.BR .pdf ,
.BR *.pdf ,
or
.B <none>
for extensionless files. May be repeated or supplied as a comma-separated list.
.TP
.BR --exclude-filetype " TYPE"
.TQ
.BR --exclude-ext " TYPE"
Exclude files with the specified extension. May be repeated or comma-separated.
.TP
.BR --include-filename " GLOB"
.TQ
.BR --include-name " GLOB"
Include filenames matching the glob. May be repeated or comma-separated.
.TP
.BR --exclude-filename " GLOB"
.TQ
.BR --exclude-name " GLOB"
Exclude filenames matching the glob. May be repeated or comma-separated.
.TP
.BR --include-foldername " GLOB"
.TQ
.BR --include-folder " GLOB"
Include files whose parent folder component or relative folder path matches the
glob. For archive members, candidates also include the archive path and member
folder path. May be repeated or comma-separated.
.TP
.BR --exclude-foldername " GLOB"
.TQ
.BR --exclude-folder " GLOB"
Exclude matching folders and their descendants. Excluded filesystem
directories are pruned and are not scanned. Matching folders inside archives
exclude only matching archive members.
.TP
.BR --format " " { txt , csv , both }
Select output format. The default is
.BR both .
.TP
.BR --output-dir " DIRECTORY"
Directory for generated reports. The default is the current directory.
.TP
.BR --basename " NAME"
Base filename without an extension. By default, a timestamped name such as
.B file_inventory_20260721_235959
is used. Paths are not accepted.
.TP
.BR --txt-path-mode " " { full , relative }
Write full or root-relative paths to the TXT report. The default is
.BR full .
.TP
.B --zip
Create a ZIP archive containing all generated reports.
.TP
.B --zip-only
Create the ZIP archive and remove the loose inventory reports. This implies
.BR --zip .
Any generated error log remains as a loose file and is also included in the
ZIP.
.TP
.B --no-archives
Do not inspect supported archives for member filenames. Archive container files
can still appear as normal filesystem results.
.TP
.B --follow-links
Follow symbolic directory links. This may cross outside the requested root or
encounter cycles; links are therefore not followed by default.
.TP
.B --case-sensitive
Use case-sensitive extension, filename, and folder matching.
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress the completion summary. Errors are never suppressed.
.TP
.B --version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Display command help and exit.
.SH ARCHIVE SUPPORT
Archive traversal is enabled by default and does not extract files.
.PP
Supported ZIP formats and containers:
.BR .zip ,
.BR .jar ,
.BR .war ,
.BR .ear ,
.BR .whl ,
.BR .apk ,
.BR .xpi ,
and
.BR .epub .
.PP
Supported TAR formats:
.BR .tar ,
.BR .tar.gz ,
.BR .tgz ,
.BR .tar.bz2 ,
.BR .tbz ,
.BR .tbz2 ,
.BR .tar.xz ,
and
.BR .txz .
.PP
Known archive formats unsupported by the dependency-free backend, including
.BR .7z ,
.BR .rar ,
.BR .cab ,
.BR .iso ,
and
.BR .tar.zst ,
are reported as failures rather than silently skipped.
.PP
Nested archive files are listed as archive members but are not recursively
opened. Filtering an archive container out of normal output does not prevent
its members from being evaluated; use
.B --no-archives
to disable member traversal entirely.
.SH OUTPUT
TXT output begins with comment lines identifying the root, generation time,
matched-file count, archive-member count, and path mode, followed by one path
per line. Archive members are prefixed with
.B [ARCHIVED]
and use a virtual path such as:
.PP
.nf
[ARCHIVED] archives/sample.zip::docs/report.pdf
.fi
.PP
CSV output contains these columns:
.BR relative_path ,
.BR full_path ,
.BR name ,
.BR extension ,
.BR parent_relative ,
.BR size_bytes ,
.BR modified_utc ,
.BR is_symlink ,
.BR is_archived ,
.BR archive_path ,
.BR archive_member_path ,
and
.BR archive_format .
.PP
ZIP member timestamps are left blank because ZIP timestamps do not reliably
carry timezone information. TAR member timestamps are written in UTC when
available.
.SH FAILURE LOGGING
Every filesystem, archive, argument, or fatal runtime failure is printed to
standard error. The program also writes a timestamped file named:
.PP
.nf
file_enum_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_microseconds_errors.txt
.fi
.PP
The error log is written under
.BR --output-dir .
If that location cannot be used, the current directory is attempted. The error
log is generated only when failures occur. It is never removed by
.BR --zip-only .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed without enumeration errors.
.TP
.B 1
The program could not run, for example because arguments were invalid, the root
path was invalid, or an output file could not be created.
.TP
.B 2
Inventory reports were created, but one or more files, directories, or archives
could not be read.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inventory a directory and supported archive contents as TXT and CSV:
.PP
.nf
file-enumerator /backup/Downloads
.fi
.PP
Include PDF and DOCX files from the filesystem and archives while pruning
dependency and cache directories:
.PP
.nf
file-enumerator /backup/Downloads \
  --include-filetype pdf,docx \
  --exclude-filename '~$*' \
  --exclude-filename '*.tmp' \
  --exclude-foldername '.git,node_modules,__pycache__' \
  --format both
.fi
.PP
Create only a ZIP archive containing relative-path reports:
.PP
.nf
file-enumerator /backup/Downloads \
  --txt-path-mode relative \
  --output-dir /backup/inventory-output \
  --basename downloads_inventory \
  --zip-only
.fi
.PP
Disable archive traversal:
.PP
.nf
file-enumerator /backup/Downloads --no-archives
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/file-enumerator
Default executable location for a source installation.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/file-enumerator.1
Default manual-page location for a source installation.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/bash-completion/completions/file-enumerator
Default Bash-completion location for a source installation.
.SH NOTES
The program intentionally excludes its prospective output files and error log
from the scan when the output directory is located beneath the enumeration
root.
.PP
The retained PowerShell implementation under
.I contrib/windows
has not yet been brought to archive feature parity with the Linux/Python
command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR find (1),
.BR tar (1),
.BR tree (1),
.BR unzip (1),
.BR zip (1)
